            "location": "jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/UnixSocketDaemonRpc.kt:97",
            "message": "Surfacing a non-empty string `result.error` as ok=false is a GLOBAL transport change (applies to every handler, not just workflow.pending). It is convention-aligned — the daemon-wide failure shape is `{ error: string }`, and no current Kotlin caller reads a success-payload `error` field as data — so it is safe today and actually corrects a latent bug where all 12 `{error}`-returning handlers were invisible as failures to the client. Recorded as an invariant to preserve: a future handler must not put a non-empty `error` string inside a SUCCESS result. Guarded correctly against over-correction (empty string / null / object error are not misclassified).",
            "confidence": "observation"
